X-WR-CALNAME:Intelligent Payroll: Austria payroll deadlines
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:at-lohnabgaben-payment@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=15
SUMMARY:Austria: Payroll taxes: Lohnsteuer\, Dienstgeberbeitrag and DB surc
 harge payment
DESCRIPTION:Wage-related levies (Lohnsteuer\, Dienstgeberbeitrag\, Zuschlag
  zum Dienstgeberbeitrag) are due on the 15th of the following month.\nAppl
 ies to: Employers in Austria\nNon-working day: Taxes due on a Saturday\, S
 unday\, public holiday\, Good Friday or 24 December are payable on the nex
 t working day.\nSource for non-working-day rule: https://www.usp.gv.at/the
 men/steuern-finanzen/steuerliche-rechte-und-pflichten/weitere-informatione
 n-zu-steuerlichen-rechten-und-pflichten-als-unternehmen/fristen-und-faelli
 gkeiten.html\n\nSource: https://www.bmf.gv.at/themen/steuern/fristen-verfa
 hren/fristen-faelligkeiten.html\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.e
 u/deadlines.html#austria\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice
 . Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holi
 days are not applied. Sources last checked 5 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#austria
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:at-kommunalsteuer-payment@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=15
SUMMARY:Austria: Kommunalsteuer (municipal payroll tax) payment
DESCRIPTION:Kommunalsteuer is among the wage-related levies that are due on
  the 15th of the following month.\nApplies to: Employers in Austria\nNon-w
 orking day: Taxes due on a Saturday\, Sunday\, public holiday\, Good Frida
 y or 24 December are payable on the next working day.\nSource for non-work
 ing-day rule: https://www.usp.gv.at/themen/steuern-finanzen/steuerliche-re
 chte-und-pflichten/weitere-informationen-zu-steuerlichen-rechten-und-pflic
 hten-als-unternehmen/fristen-und-faelligkeiten.html\n\nSource: https://www
 .bmf.gv.at/themen/steuern/fristen-verfahren/fristen-faelligkeiten.html\nDe
 tails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#austria\n\nFor inf
 ormation only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule s
 tated by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last 
 checked 5 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#austria
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:at-sv-mbgm@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=15
SUMMARY:Austria: Monthly contribution base report (mBGM) to health insuranc
 e fund
DESCRIPTION:In the self-assessment procedure the mBGM is submitted by the 1
 5th after the end of each contribution period. If employment starts after 
 the 15th\, the deadline is the 15th of the month after next.\nApplies to: 
 Employers in the self-assessment procedure (Selbstabrechner)\nNon-working-
 day rule: check the source.\n\nSource: https://www.oegk.at/cdscontent/?con
 tentid=10007.905072&portal=oegkdgportal\nDetails: https://www.intelligentp
 ayroll.eu/deadlines.html#austria\n\nFor information only\, not legal or ta
 x advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends 
 and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 5 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#austria
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:at-sv-contributions-payment@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=15
SUMMARY:Austria: Social insurance contributions payment (ÖGK)
DESCRIPTION:General contributions fall due on the last day of the calendar 
 month in which the contribution period ends. They count as paid on time if
  credited within 15 days after that due date\, which means by the 15th of 
 the following month.\nApplies to: Employers paying contributions to the he
 alth insurance fund\nNon-working day: If the last day of the 15-day period
  falls on a Saturday\, Sunday\, public holiday\, Good Friday or 24 Decembe
 r\, the period extends to the next bank working day.\nSource for non-worki
 ng-day rule: https://www.oegk.at/cdscontent/?contentid=10007.905055&portal
 =oegkdgportal\n\nSource: https://www.oegk.at/cdscontent/?contentid=10007.9
 05055&portal=oegkdgportal\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/dead
 lines.html#austria\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Date
 s follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays a
 re not applied. Sources last checked 5 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#austria
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:at-lohnzettel-annual@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270228
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270301
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=2;BYMONTHDAY=-1
SUMMARY:Austria: Annual wage statements (Lohnzettel) to the tax office
DESCRIPTION:After the calendar year the employer must send the Lohnzettel f
 or each employee electronically via ELDA\, in principle by the end of Febr
 uary of the following year.\nApplies to: Employers in Austria\nNon-working
 -day rule: check the source.\n\nSource: https://www.bmf.gv.at/themen/steue
 rn/fristen-verfahren/fristen-faelligkeiten.html\nDetails: https://www.inte
 lligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#austria\n\nFor information only\, not leg
 al or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; w
 eekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 5 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#austria
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
